    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99-a2">

                <pb facs="0271" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg261"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2 in No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Commander Baldwin, U. S. N., to Sir P. Wodehouse.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Vanderbilt, Cape
                            Town,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to make known to your
                    excellency the arrival here of this ship.</p>
                <p>I have come to this harbor for the purpose of making some necessary repairs to my
                    meahinery, and also to get a supply of fuel.</p>
                <p>I therefore ask your excellency’s permission to lie here for the above-mentioned
                    purposes the necessary time, say, from four to six working days.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHAS. K BALDWIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
